<title>HONG KONG: New World Dev 1995/96 net up 21.89 pct.</title>
<headline>New World Dev 1995/96 net up 21.89 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>		(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   244.0	  vs 211.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    84.0	   vs 78.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  1,148.6 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    4,157.7	vs 3,410.9</p>
<p>    Turnover		     16,715.5     vs 17,456.7</p>
<p>    Company name		 New World Development Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 13-20, 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 27, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - New World Development engages in investment holding, property investment and development, construction and hotel investment.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on partial disposal of and dilution of investment in subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Final dividend of 84 H.K. cents per share comprising minimum cash dividend of one cent per share, and an issue of additional shares by way of scrip dividend equivalent to 83 cents per share with a cash option.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 114 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 30 cents) vs 106 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
